# Accessibility (target state)

New and heavily edited interactive UI must be usable by keyboard and announce state to assistive tech.

## Minimums

- **Dialogs:** `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal`, labelled title, Escape closes (follow `Modal.tsx`)
- **Tabs:** prefer `tablist` / `tab` / `aria-selected` / `aria-controls` when rewriting tab chrome - do not invent mouse-only tab strips
- **Icon-only buttons:** meaningful `aria-label`
- **Errors / toasts:** `role="alert"` or `aria-live="polite"` for important async feedback
- **Forms:** associate labels (`Label` + input ids); do not rely on placeholder-only labeling

## Avoid

- Mouse-only drag-and-drop without a keyboard alternative for critical assignment flows
- Decorative SVG/diagram controls without accessible names when they are the primary scoring affordance
- Shipping color-only status (always pair with text/icon)

Do not depend on an a11y plugin being present - bake the contract into components as you touch them.
